KG42.register("nodes-91bebeb26e449d4fa5077e25",{"id":"COMP-9ca8822ee86e3e13","code":"PRC010","label":"Uniform last-accepted-bid pricing, experimental fixed prices and proposed per-trade bid pricing","definition":"This unit contains three pricing definitions in parallel: the stated double auction sets p^{clear}_t = p^{last}_t and forms a time-interval uniform price; the three-month trial sets p^{trial}_t = p̄_trial and uses a predetermined fixed price; the proposed pay-as-you bid order book allows transaction-by-transaction prices. Each definition is limited to its corresponding context.","layer":"L6","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"pricing.local","concept_ids":["pricing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: unit price of local energy transactions","Parallel operations: pricing at the last awarded bid, preset fixed pricing, and transaction-by-transaction pricing","Output: the respectively applicable time-interval uniform price, trial fixed price, or transaction-by-transaction price"]},"exclusions":["The double auction uses 15-minute time intervals.","The fixed-price trial had only one consumer and one prosumer, and the auction was not actually enabled.","The trial price is the Brooklyn conventional renewable energy price.","pay-as-you bid is a proposed follow-up trial.","General recommendation: lower prices for surplus energy and raise prices for energy shortage; socioeconomic preferences may cause the local price to be higher than the grid price.","Additional energy may use a preset price.","The market price can be displayed to EMTS and used for payment, but these uses do not define the pricing algorithm."],"members":[{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Submitted buy orders provide requested quantities and bid prices to local clearing, which allocates the highest bidder first and then lower bidders. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Submitted sell orders provide offered quantities and prices to the market mechanism responsible for local energy allocation. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Matching participants' buy and sell orders is specified as the means of achieving efficient local energy allocation. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price receive additional energy allocated through a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. Scope: BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers Condition: Consumers do not undercut the clearing price. Minimum and maximum energy-allocation constraints should exist, especially to account for prosumer generation constraints. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Different market time horizons should ideally be implemented, and allocation mechanisms must be tailored to achieve efficient allocation at each stage. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons Local energy allocation should preferably operate at near-real-time granularity. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Local clearing uses a closed order book and a time-discrete double auction in 15-minute slots. Scope: BMG specified double-auction mechanism","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers | BMG specified double-auction mechanism | BMG specified local double-auction mechanism | General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons | General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e35"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1bbe8c3fe342874c6a3359fb3aba730cc3386f72459200ac03dd4f4c78b1f84b","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Local market price information informs decentralized trading decisions, and EMTS may respond to variable prices through demand-side management. Scope: General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. For the illustrative simple EMTS, the decentralized decision to buy energy on the microgrid market is triggered whenever the market price falls below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the EMTS's maximum price limit. Price signals should indicate energy scarcity or surplus. Scope: General microgrid market price-signal design.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. | General microgrid market price-signal design. | Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"4b4dbcdf1deae944a3339a8f6be08b7f348f8d9de35c43da93d2800719bc6c35","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, purchasing energy on the microgrid market is conditioned on the local market price falling below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the simple EMTS's maximum price limit. Local trading is conducted only virtually on the blockchain and does not influence the physical delivery of electricity. Scope: BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. Automatic trading requires participant preferences, such as preferred energy sources and price limits. Scope: BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. Condition: Automatic trading by the EMTS. The EMTS must have access to its market participant's blockchain account to facilitate energy transactions automatically. Scope: Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. Condition: Energy transactions are facilitated automatically by the EMTS.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. | BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. | BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. | Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-e023"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"12304e5e73e5aa8aa94847a8499fbb19352d81dde95c27d5c00990b5c6e6324c","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","market_meaning":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used. A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used. Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus. A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking. The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered. The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used. Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. | BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. | BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. | BMG stated time-slot pricing design. | General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. | General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g03-e016"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"e5dc359e0f8848970cafe680480a92663cbc24c7dcee3b49ef9157fafdfb1042","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","market_meaning":"Local allocation supplies the allocated participants between whom financial transactions are carried out according to predefined payment rules. Scope: BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. The local transaction price determined by the pricing mechanism is used for monetary payment; the illustrated BMG payment rules use the clearing price. Scope: Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules. Payment is carried out once counterparty matching is completed. Scope: BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. Condition: Matching has been completed. Consumers pay their producing neighbors for feeding renewable generation into the distribution grid. Scope: Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. Condition: Producing neighbors feed renewable generation into the distribution grid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. | BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. | Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. | Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35","v141-b-g03-e022"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"cbcdd5e0a18793905b4452d98d282abe6114cf83dee8226cbc4b4d7be776a3c1","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["24-brooklyn_microgrid"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26].","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the TransActive Grid private blockchain protocol (C3). Thus, the characteristics of data consistency, security, and verification are covered by the TransActive Grid platform and are inherited traits from the blockchain protocol. Based on measurements of demand and supply as well as market information, the platform tracks and displays local (near) real time energy prices on an intuitive interface. Thus, market participants may gather generation, consumption and market information, and trade energy needs accordingly. Trading is mostly done automatically by the EMTS (C6) and just requires several preferences of its market participants, e.g. the preferred energy sources and price limits.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the TransActive Grid private blockchain protocol (C3). Thus, the characteristics of data consistency, security, and verification are covered by the TransActive Grid platform and are inherited traits from the blockchain protocol. Based on measurements of demand and supply as well as market information, the platform tracks and displays local (near) real time energy prices on an intuitive interface. Thus, market participants may gather generation, consumption and market information, and trade energy needs accordingly. Trading is mostly done automatically by the EMTS (C6) and just requires several preferences of its market participants, e.g. the preferred energy sources and price limits."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26].","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented. Hence, C4 and C5 are sufﬁciently addressed for operation.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented. Hence, C4 and C5 are sufﬁciently addressed for operation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"C1 U The BMG clearly aims at increasing the local security of energy supply and at strengthening the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"C1 U The BMG clearly aims at increasing the local security of energy supply and at strengthening the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4 (U) The initial mechanism is a double auction mechanism. C5 (U) A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics. C6 (U) Residents set their price limits for local renewable energy and choose their generation mix.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"C4 (U) The initial mechanism is a double auction mechanism. C5 (U) A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics. C6 (U) Residents set their price limits for local renewable energy and choose their generation mix."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e016","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and ﬁxed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented. Hence, although the market and pricing mechanism are implemented and operational, they have not yet been tested in extended real-life trial runs. In conclusion, we judge C4 and C5 to be only partly addressed by the BMG.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and ﬁxed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented. Hence, although the market and pricing mechanism are implemented and operational, they have not yet been tested in extended real-life trial runs. In conclusion, we judge C4 and C5 to be only partly addressed by the BMG."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. High-level topo currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In addition to the currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efﬁciency before determining the ﬁnal market mechanism.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"In addition to the currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efﬁciency before determining the ﬁnal market mechanism."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e024","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. High-level topo currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efficiency before determining the final market mechanism.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efficiency before determining the final market mechanism."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU).","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU).","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Sell Orders: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); Buy Order: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); x_clearing","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"Sell Orders: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); Buy Order: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); x_clearing"}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["multiple_price_formation_rules"],"projection_statuses":["composite"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L6-7afa02ac0a","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L6","ontological_kind":"composite_rule"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Submitted buy orders provide requested quantities and bid prices to local clearing, which allocates the highest bidder first and then lower bidders. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Submitted sell orders provide offered quantities and prices to the market mechanism responsible for local energy allocation. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Matching participants' buy and sell orders is specified as the means of achieving efficient local energy allocation. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price receive additional energy allocated through a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. Scope: BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers Condition: Consumers do not undercut the clearing price. Minimum and maximum energy-allocation constraints should exist, especially to account for prosumer generation constraints. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Different market time horizons should ideally be implemented, and allocation mechanisms must be tailored to achieve efficient allocation at each stage. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons Local energy allocation should preferably operate at near-real-time granularity. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Local clearing uses a closed order book and a time-discrete double auction in 15-minute slots. Scope: BMG specified double-auction mechanism","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers | BMG specified double-auction mechanism | BMG specified local double-auction mechanism | General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons | General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e35"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1bbe8c3fe342874c6a3359fb3aba730cc3386f72459200ac03dd4f4c78b1f84b"},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Local market price information informs decentralized trading decisions, and EMTS may respond to variable prices through demand-side management. Scope: General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. For the illustrative simple EMTS, the decentralized decision to buy energy on the microgrid market is triggered whenever the market price falls below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the EMTS's maximum price limit. Price signals should indicate energy scarcity or surplus. Scope: General microgrid market price-signal design.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. | General microgrid market price-signal design. | Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"4b4dbcdf1deae944a3339a8f6be08b7f348f8d9de35c43da93d2800719bc6c35"},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, purchasing energy on the microgrid market is conditioned on the local market price falling below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the simple EMTS's maximum price limit. Local trading is conducted only virtually on the blockchain and does not influence the physical delivery of electricity. Scope: BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. Automatic trading requires participant preferences, such as preferred energy sources and price limits. Scope: BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. Condition: Automatic trading by the EMTS. The EMTS must have access to its market participant's blockchain account to facilitate energy transactions automatically. Scope: Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. Condition: Energy transactions are facilitated automatically by the EMTS.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. | BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. | BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. | Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-e023"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"12304e5e73e5aa8aa94847a8499fbb19352d81dde95c27d5c00990b5c6e6324c"},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","market_meaning":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used. A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used. Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus. A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking. The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered. The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used. Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. | BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. | BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. | BMG stated time-slot pricing design. | General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. | General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g03-e016"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"e5dc359e0f8848970cafe680480a92663cbc24c7dcee3b49ef9157fafdfb1042"},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","market_meaning":"Local allocation supplies the allocated participants between whom financial transactions are carried out according to predefined payment rules. Scope: BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. The local transaction price determined by the pricing mechanism is used for monetary payment; the illustrated BMG payment rules use the clearing price. Scope: Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules. Payment is carried out once counterparty matching is completed. Scope: BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. Condition: Matching has been completed. Consumers pay their producing neighbors for feeding renewable generation into the distribution grid. Scope: Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. Condition: Producing neighbors feed renewable generation into the distribution grid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. | BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. | Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. | Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35","v141-b-g03-e022"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"cbcdd5e0a18793905b4452d98d282abe6114cf83dee8226cbc4b4d7be776a3c1"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price receive additional energy allocated through a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. Scope: BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers Condition: Consumers do not undercut the clearing price.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local market price information informs decentralized trading decisions, and EMTS may respond to variable prices through demand-side management. Scope: General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the TransActive Grid private blockchain protocol (C3). Thus, the characteristics of data consistency, security, and verification are covered by the TransActive Grid platform and are inherited traits from the blockchain protocol. Based on measurements of demand and supply as well as market information, the platform tracks and displays local (near) real time energy prices on an intuitive interface. Thus, market participants may gather generation, consumption and market information, and trade energy needs accordingly. Trading is mostly done automatically by the EMTS (C6) and just requires several preferences of its market participants, e.g. the preferred energy sources and price limits."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, the decentralized decision to buy energy on the microgrid market is triggered whenever the market price falls below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the EMTS's maximum price limit.","expression":"p_M \u003c p_i_max => buy_i = 1","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta001","v141-c-R005-theta002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, purchasing energy on the microgrid market is conditioned on the local market price falling below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the simple EMTS's maximum price limit.","expression":"p_{\\mathrm{local}} \u003c p_{\\max} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; b = 1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_R006_buy"],"parameter_refs":["theta_R006_p_local","theta_R006_p_max"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used.","expression":"p^{\\mathrm{clear}}_t = p^{\\mathrm{last}}_t \\quad \\text{(for the time slot } t\\text{; the resulting uniform clearing price applies to transactions in that slot)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_clear_t","x_last_bid_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g03-e009"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented. Hence, C4 and C5 are sufﬁciently addressed for operation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g02-e14"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"C1 U The BMG clearly aims at increasing the local security of energy supply and at strengthening the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"C1 U The BMG clearly aims at increasing the local security of energy supply and at strengthening the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4 (U) The initial mechanism is a double auction mechanism. C5 (U) A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics. C6 (U) Residents set their price limits for local renewable energy and choose their generation mix."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used.","expression":"p^{\\mathrm{trial}}_t = \\bar{p}_{\\mathrm{trial}} \\quad \\text{(fixed during the reported three-month trial period)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_trial_price_t"],"parameter_refs":["theta_trial_fixed_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g02-e15"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e016","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and ﬁxed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented. Hence, although the market and pricing mechanism are implemented and operational, they have not yet been tested in extended real-life trial runs. In conclusion, we judge C4 and C5 to be only partly addressed by the BMG."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e024"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. High-level topo currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In addition to the currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efﬁciency before determining the ﬁnal market mechanism."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e024","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. High-level topo currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efficiency before determining the final market mechanism."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local transaction price determined by the pricing mechanism is used for monetary payment; the illustrated BMG payment rules use the clearing price. Scope: Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e30"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"In the illustrated BMG payment rules, consumer C1 is annotated as paying producer P24 and consumer C5 as paying producer P22, with the clearing price x_clearing shown above the arrow and the allocated quantity min{y_1,y_24} or min{y_5,y_22} shown below the arrow. The source presents this arrow annotation rather than a separately written payment-amount equation.","expression":"C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24};\\quad C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","matching.counterparties","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_x_clearing","theta_y_consumer","theta_y_producer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Sell Orders: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); Buy Order: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); x_clearing"}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x001","symbol":"buy_i","meaning":"Decentralized purchase decision of EMTS/market participant i for the illustrative simple EMTS strategy; 1 denotes buying energy on the microgrid market and 0 denotes not buying. The source describes the action but provides no explicit mathematical symbol.","kind":"operational","domain":"binary {0,1}; formalized purchase action, source gives no explicit notation","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x001"},{"variable_id":"x_R006_buy","symbol":"b","meaning":"Binary purchase-execution decision of the simple EMTS on the microgrid market; b=1 denotes that the simple EMTS executes a purchase at the activation decision.","kind":"operational","domain":"{0,1}","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::x::x_R006_buy"},{"variable_id":"x_clear_t","symbol":"p^{\\mathrm{clear}}_t","meaning":"Uniform market clearing price for time slot t; the source identifies this price with the last allocated bid price and says double-auction clearing occurs at uniform prices.","kind":"operational","domain":"Local time-slot price; the source does not state a numeric range in the supplied rule evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g03-e009","v141-b-g03-e010"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::x::x_clear_t"},{"variable_id":"x_last_bid_t","symbol":"p^{\\mathrm{last}}_t","meaning":"Price of the last allocated bid in time slot t, i.e. the price-setting last allocated bid.","kind":"operational","domain":"Bid price in the local order book; the source does not state a numeric range in the supplied rule evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::x::x_last_bid_t"},{"variable_id":"x_trial_price_t","symbol":"p^{\\mathrm{trial}}_t","meaning":"Electricity price applied during the reported three-month trial, which the source says was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn.","kind":"operational","domain":"Trial-period electricity price; the numeric value and range are not stated.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g02-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::x::x_trial_price_t"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta001","symbol":"p_M","meaning":"Microgrid local market energy price observed by the EMTS when applying the simple buying rule; descriptive symbol because the supplied text gives no explicit notation.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta002","symbol":"p_i_max","meaning":"Maximum price limit of EMTS/market participant i for buying energy on the microgrid market; descriptive symbol because the supplied text gives no explicit notation.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002"},{"parameter_id":"theta_R006_p_local","symbol":"p_{\\mathrm{local}}","meaning":"Local microgrid market price at the activation decision, referred to in the source as the microgrid market price or 'the price'.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::theta::theta_R006_p_local"},{"parameter_id":"theta_R006_p_max","symbol":"p_{\\max}","meaning":"Maximum price limit of the simple EMTS, described by the source as 'its maximum price limit'; a participant-specific preference threshold.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::theta::theta_R006_p_max"},{"parameter_id":"theta_trial_fixed_price","symbol":"\\bar{p}_{\\mathrm{trial}}","meaning":"Predetermined fixed electricity price during the three-month trial, set at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g02-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::theta::theta_trial_fixed_price"},{"parameter_id":"theta_x_clearing","symbol":"x_{\\text{clearing}}","meaning":"Clearing price for the time slot used as the transaction price in the illustrated BMG payment-rule annotation. The quoted payment annotation does not give a separate formula for how the clearing price is determined.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"x_{\\text{clearing}}"},"unit":"MU/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::theta::theta_x_clearing"},{"parameter_id":"theta_y_consumer","symbol":"y_i","meaning":"Order quantity submitted by a consumer i, used in the payment annotation's allocated quantity min{y_i,y_j}; the source presents y_1 and y_5 as instances.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"y_i"},"unit":"kWh","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_consumer"},{"parameter_id":"theta_y_producer","symbol":"y_j","meaning":"Order quantity offered by a prosumer j, used in the payment annotation's allocated quantity min{y_i,y_j}; the source presents y_24 and y_22 as instances.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"y_j"},"unit":"kWh","indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_producer"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"multiple_price_formation_rules","projection_status":"composite","target_definition":"This unit contains three pricing definitions in parallel: the stated double auction sets p^{clear}_t = p^{last}_t and forms a time-interval uniform price; the three-month trial sets p^{trial}_t = p̄_trial and uses a predetermined fixed price; the proposed pay-as-you bid order book allows transaction-by-transaction prices. Each definition is limited to its corresponding context.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: unit price of local energy transactions","Parallel operations: pricing at the last awarded bid, preset fixed pricing, and transaction-by-transaction pricing","Output: the respectively applicable time-interval uniform price, trial fixed price, or transaction-by-transaction price"],"variation_fields":["The double auction uses 15-minute time intervals.","The fixed-price trial had only one consumer and one prosumer, and the auction was not actually enabled.","The trial price is the Brooklyn conventional renewable energy price.","pay-as-you bid is a proposed follow-up trial.","General recommendation: lower prices for surplus energy and raise prices for energy shortage; socioeconomic preferences may cause the local price to be higher than the grid price.","Additional energy may use a preset price.","The market price can be displayed to EMTS and used for payment, but these uses do not define the pricing algorithm."],"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C004","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C005","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C006","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C007","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C004","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002"],"paper_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/189"});
